Google robots.txt test cases (vendored)

cases.json is derived from robots_test.cc of https://github.com/google/robotstxt
(commit 22b355ff855419e6a3ff8ff09c0ad7fdb17116f9), Copyright 2019 Google LLC,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory).

Changes: every EXPECT_TRUE/EXPECT_FALSE(IsUserAgentAllowed(robotstxt, agent, url))
assertion of the tests in that file was converted mechanically into one JSON object
{test, robotstxt, agent, url, allowed}. Tests that do not call IsUserAgentAllowed
(user-agent validity, parser line/BOM reporting, sitemap reporting, path/escape helpers)
and GoogleOnly_LineTooLong (built with absl::StrCat) are not included; they are listed
in "skipped_tests" or covered by own tests in crates/vc-policy/tests/robots.rs.
No expectation was changed. Cases where VoyagerBot deliberately differs are listed with
their reason in crates/vc-policy/tests/robots.rs (KNOWN_DEVIATIONS).
